{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And she opened it and saw him — the child — the commentator (Rashi) who explained that she saw the child is mistaken. For who does not know that if she opened the ark she would see the child?! Rather, this is its meaning: she opened the ark and looked at the child, whether male or female, and saw that he was a נער — that is, this child is male and not female, and she saw by his maleness that he is circumcised, and therefore he was hidden away and is not an foundling; for if it were a girl, one could say he is a foundling. And likewise we find written: מה נעשה לנער היולד — on the day of birth he is called נער." "And behold, a נער crying, and she had compassion on him, etc. — because he was crying, therefore ותחמול עליו — and because she saw him a male, circumcised, she said: מילדי העברית זה. A parallel to this: ולחנה יתן מנה אחת אפים, a choice portion. And why? כי את חנה אהב. Therefore he gave her from the portion before him. If so, why מנה אחת? כי יהוה סגר רחמה — but to Peninnah and to all her sons and daughters he gave many portions, for she had many children. ותראהו את הילד והנה נער בוכה."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:38.003949862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}